From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 2 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.153
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.153 V19.0.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  Network-Congestion-Area-Report (4101): Grouped, 2 members, clause 5.3.2
  Ns-Request-Type (4102): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.3

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..284aa68 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -8873,6 +8873,15 @@
 		<avp name="SCS-Realm" code="3942" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" protected="may" vendor-id="TGPP">
 			<type type-name="DiameterIdentity"/>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="Network-Congestion-Area-Report" code="4101" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="yes" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="Network-Area-Info-List"/>
+				<gavp name="Congestion-Level-Value"/>
+			</grouped>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="Ns-Request-Type" code="4102" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="yes" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
 
 		<!--
 		Note: The AVP codes from 3900 to 3999 are reserved for TS 32.299
